To: @ViewBag.To
From: Inputlog <inputlog@uantwerpen.be />
Subject: Inputlog personal code
<html>
<head><title></title></head>
<body>
    <table style="width:775px;background-color:#e5e5e5;">
        <tr style="height:11px;width:100%;">
        </tr>
        <tr style="height:11px;width:100%;">
            <td style="width:90px;"></td>
            <td style="background-color:#fff; padding:16px 20px">
                <img src="https://www.inputlog.net/images/Home_picture.gif" alt="Inputlog header" />
                <p style="padding:8px 20px; font-size:10.5pt; line-height:125%; font-family:'Calibri','sans-serif'; color:#17375e;">
                    Dear @ViewBag.Username,<br />
                    <br />
                    Thank you for your interest in Inputlog. Your research project sounds very interesting.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    We are happy to send you a personal installation code: <b>IL7558</b>
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    Your account on the Inputlog analysis server has now been activated as well. 
                    You can log in via <a href="@ViewBag.Link">this link</a>.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    On the Inputlog <a href="https://www.inputlog.net/">website</a> you will find some additional 
                    information and also a FAQ-section about installing and using the program. A good way to start using Inputlog is watching the demonstration video. The website is regularly updated with new versions and information about presentations at conferences and workshops.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    Please note that at this moment Inputlog is a beta version. The logging and most analyses work fine. 
                    However, some functions  require more debugging. If you want to rely on the replay we advise you to use an additional screencam like Camstudio or Camtasia. New version releases will appear regularly on the Inputlog website.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    Keystroke logging data are always bound to the assessment skills of the researcher.
                    We therefore recommend you to use the automatic analyses like Summary analyses in order to get a 
                    first impression of the data. Further coding and manual analyses are best done on the General logging file. 
                    This gives you optimal control over your analyses. You can find more information about measures and analyzing
                    techniques on the <a href="https://www.writingpro.eu/">WritingPro</a> website.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    We wish you all the best with your research. If you have any further questions, please, 
                    don't hesitate to contact us. We appreciate if you keep us informed about your research.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    Kind regards
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    Luuk Van Waes
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    PS: Please note that Inputlog is a research instrument that is free to the research community. We strongly believe in sharing information like research techniques etc. Therefore, we would like to encourage you to provide information on your research project via <a href="https://www.writingpro.eu/">WritingPro</a>.
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    <br />
                    <a href="https://www.inputlog.net">Inputlog.net</a>
                    <br />
                    <br />
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="width:90px;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="height:11px;width:100%;">
        </tr>
    </table>
</body>
</html>